NAME
       xfs_admin - show or change the label and UUID of an XFS file system

SYNOPSIS
       xfs_admin [-l] [-u] [-L LABEL] [-U UUID] DEVICE

DESCRIPTION
       xfs_admin changes settings of an XFS file system. The file system
       must be unmounted for changes (-L, -U). For ext file systems use
       tune2fs or e2label instead.

OPTIONS
       -l     Print the label.

       -u     Print the UUID.

       -L LABEL
              Set the label (up to 12 characters). -L -- removes it.

       -U UUID
              Set the UUID: a value, generate (a new random one), or nil.

EXAMPLES
       Give the XFS file system on /dev/vdb1 the label archive and mount it
       by label at boot:

           umount /dev/vdb1
           xfs_admin -L archive /dev/vdb1
           echo 'LABEL=archive /archive xfs defaults 0 0' >> /etc/fstab
           mount -a

SEE ALSO
       mkfs.xfs(8), xfs_info(8), blkid(8), tune2fs(8), fstab(5)
